/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  extract03_acetic_acid_mibk_perry  --  Perry's Example 15-1 on the extractor

  WHAT IT IS.  The problem of Perry's Chemical Engineers' Handbook (9th ed.,
  Example 15-1, p. 15-48): 100 kg/h of 20 wt% acetic acid in water extracted
  with 200 kg/h of recycle methyl isobutyl ketone (0.1 wt% acid, 0.01 wt%
  water) at 25 C, in a countercurrent cascade of theoretical stages.  Perry
  reads 4.3 stages from his shortcut (Eq. 15-43) and from a McCabe-Thiele plot
  on the MEASURED equilibrium of Table 15-8 (raffinate to 1 wt% acid).

  WHAT THE ENGINE DOES WITH IT.  Five stages, each the liquid-liquid flash of
  the case's package (UNIFAC, nothing fitted).  The unit prints its own
  Kremser-Souders-Brown CHECK beside the rigorous count (KPIs N_shortcut,
  E_shortcut, Kp_*): Perry's formula on K' = Y/X read from the two end stages
  the cascade itself solved.  And a DECLARED HETS turns the stage count into
  a column height (KPI height_m) -- a rating on the case's own number.

  WHAT IT IS NOT.  Not a validation of the cascade: the case that holds the
  package against Perry's measured tie lines is
  tutorials/props/compare/lle01_acetic_mibk_perry, and it finds UNIFAC
  over-predicts the acid taken up by the MIBK and the water that dissolves in
  it, so this cascade removes MORE acid than Perry's measured system would at
  the same N.  The HETS below is an ILLUSTRATIVE number to show the arithmetic,
  declared as such; no source ships it (Perry's Sec. 15 tabulates HETS by
  column type -- read the one for the column you mean).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        extractor01;
        type        extractor;
        inputs      ( feed  solvent );        // feed at stage 1, solvent at stage N
        outputs     ( extract  raffinate );   // extract leaves stage 1, raffinate stage N

        operation
        {
            stages       5;
            solvent      methylIsobutylKetone;
            temperature  25 degC;
            hets         1.5 m;
            hetsSource   "ILLUSTRATIVE value declared by the tutorial to show N x HETS; not a design number";
        }
    }
);
